st we just we wanted to end the  suffering our families and we wanted  them to get nothing but and you thought  if you didn't succeed they wouldn't kill  you the next day throughout the  captivity they made it very clear they  would kill tahun Assad first and that  hatred towards Afghans and Pakistanis  that work with the United States is much  deeper than the hatred towards Americans  and they constantly said and this has  happened in past cases there was a  kidnapping an Italian journalist where  they killed the driver  later and then you know got a larger  ransom for the journalists so I didn't  feeling that much danger one member of  the economy family kept calling me the  golden hen expecting me play at a go  away which was never late and I'm so  happy and lucky to be here yeah you're  very clear in the article and the times  has been very clear that no ransom was  paid yet there's still some skepticism  sure out in the world about that i think  if some people find it hard to believe  that your captors just slept through the  night without any incentives i expect  you to repeat your denial but how does  it weigh how do you confront the  skepticism just that I don't know I  would never write a five part series  that was a lot just personally and this  newspaper would never run a series based  on a lot but I lived through and I know  what to hear lived through I've talked  ad nauseam to the Pakistani this young  captain lettuce on his base that night  no one was in the area he had no idea we  were coming it took them and I think it  took them eight or nine hours to get in  a helicopter to move us out of the base  and I know there's skepticism out there  but no money was paid there's been some  writing about an earlier plan and our  kidnapping to try to bribe our guards  there was information coming in about a  village we were being held in we were  never held in that village and you know  attempts were made to dragon information  while we were being held but they